    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="lblTrust">
     <property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property>
     <property name="text"><string>Yellowback is a miner-enforced, over-collateralised stablecoin overlay on Ycash. Every Ycash node enforces that collateral cannot leave a vault before its lock height and that only the minter's key can spend it before the claim height. The rest — collateral released only against the burn of the vault's debt — is enforced by the mining pools that run the Yellowback module: a majority of hashpower that runs the module and follows it makes those rules hold; a majority that does not could release collateral without burns or move the price, as it could already reorganise the chain. Prices are medians of the quotes pools publish in their own blocks. YED is transparent: balances and transfers are visible on the chain; it is not a shielded asset.</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
  </layout>
